                <pb facs="0452" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7251: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-26T16:00:00+03:00">August 26, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 26—12:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>389. Doctor Yen, Chinese Ambassador, stated to me yesterday that his latest
                    information from Nanking indicated that the Chinese Government felt compelled to
                    accept the Japanese demand for “full economic cooperation”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
